{
  "rationale": "Each test implements the intent from the plan, using only the specification to justify the claim. For tests that compute the correct answer directly (like prefix_sum, greedy_left, greedy_right), they are limited to small n (≤500) to stay fast. Bounds tests (lower_bound_excess, upper_bound_trivial) apply to all inputs. Format and sanity checks (non_negative, integer_format, newline) enforce the output format. All_equal_zero and n1_zero are direct consequences of the problem statement. The weakest test is likely test_greedy_right because it is redundant with test_greedy_left given the specification; I would drop it first if needed.",
