{
  "rationale": "We include basic output format, ordering, and distinctness checks. Polynomial evaluation and Vieta's formulas verify algebraic correctness. Direct computation with high precision is the most reliable test. Bounds and finiteness catch extreme errors. Discriminant consistency ensures proper spacing between roots. If we had to drop one, we would drop the bounds test as it is least likely to catch a subtle backdoor.",
  "plan": [
    {
      "name": "test_format",
