}

{
  "rationale": "The tests combine direct simulation for small inputs (all given have n ≤ 13) with necessary conditions that any correct answer must satisfy. Direct simulation (test_correct) is the strongest catch. Bounds, format, and invariants like monotone side, all-U/all-R, sign changes, gate visit bound, side-tracking consistency, prefix monotonicity, and parity with start/end sides provide overlapping coverage. Each test is justified by the specification alone. If a test must be dropped, test_parity is the least general because it only applies when the final position is not a gate.",
