{
  "rationale": "The tests include a brute-force verification for small strings (length ≤10) to catch any wrong answer on the given inputs. Basic sanity checks ensure the output is a valid integer within [1, n] and respects obvious bounds: at least the longest alternating run in the original string (since zero operations are allowed) and at most n. Special cases: monochrome strings must output 1; already alternating strings must output n. Combinatorial upper bounds from color counts and from the doubled string (since any cyclic shift appears in s+s) are also enforced. Finally, if both colors appear, at least a length-2 zebra is always achievable via an appropriate cyclic shift. These tests are derived directly from the problem statement and hold for any correct solution. If forced to drop one, the brute-force test would be the first to go as it is limited to small n.",
  "plan": [
    {
      "name": "test_bruteforce_small",
      "intent": "For inputs of length at most 10, compute the exact maximum zebra length by exploring all strings reachable via the allowed operations (BFS over states) and assert the output equals that value. If the input is longer, skip."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_output_range",
      "intent": "Assert that the output parses as an integer and lies between 1 and the length of the input string inclusive. A violation would be a non-integer or a number outside this range."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_lower_bound_original",
      "intent": "Compute the length of the longest contiguous alternating substring in the original input string. Assert that the output is at least that length, because doing zero operations yields that substring. A violation would be an output smaller than this lower bound."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_upper_bound_n",
      "intent": "Assert that the output is at most the length of the input string, since any zebra is a contiguous selection of pieces from a string of that length. A violation would be an output exceeding the string length."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_monochrome",
      "intent": "If all characters in the input are the same ('b' or 'w'), assert that the output is exactly 1, because no alternating substring longer than 1 can be formed. A violation would be any other value."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_alternating",
      "intent": "If the input string has no two consecutive equal characters (i.e., it alternates), assert that the output equals the length of the string, since the whole string is already an alternating zebra. A violation would be a different value."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_upper_bound_counts",
      "intent": "Count the number of 'b' and 'w' characters. The output cannot exceed 2 * min(count_b, count_w) + (1 if counts differ else 0), because an alternating substring of length L uses at least floor(L/2) of each color and one color possibly one more. A violation would be an output exceeding this bound."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_upper_bound_doubled",
      "intent": "Compute the longest contiguous alternating substring in the string concatenated with itself (s+s). Assert that the output is at most that length, because any cyclic shift of the input (which is reachable) appears as a substring of s+s and thus its longest alternating substring is a substring of s+s. A violation would be an output greater than that."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_lower_bound_two_colors",
      "intent": "If the input contains both 'b' and 'w' at least once, assert that the output is at least 2. This is always achievable by an appropriate cyclic shift that places a b next to a w. A violation would be an output of 1 when both colors are present."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_output_format",
      "intent": "Assert that the output string consists of a single integer, optionally followed by a newline, with no other characters (no extra whitespace). Specifically, after stripping trailing newline, the string must be convertible to an integer and must contain only digits. A violation would be extra spaces, letters, or multiple numbers."
    }
  ]
}

