  "rationale": "The submission may contain a backdoor that reduces registration numbers modulo 997, causing collisions and underestimates of the required capacity. These tests check necessary conditions that any correct answer must satisfy, with a focus on catching underestimates. The exact verification (test 1) is the strongest; others provide bounds and feasibility checks. Test 7 directly targets collisions by demanding that the output be at least the per-residue required capacity. Tests 8–9 add combinatorial bounds, and test 10 handles the all-exit special case. All tests are derived from the specification and hold for every valid input.",
