{
  "rationale": "The tests verify properties of the diamond pattern as implied by the specification. The exact match test recomputes the expected output from the geometric definition, catching any deviation. Shape tests ensure correct dimensions and character set. Symmetry tests (palindrome, vertical symmetry) and D-count tests (per row, total) check structural invariants that the backdoor for n=9 would violate. If one test had to be dropped, test_characters would be the first, as it is the weakest and largely covered by other tests.",
