  "rationale": "Each test implements one intent from the plan, adjusted to be justified solely by the specification and to work on all given inputs. Strengths: test_format and test_range are direct from output spec. test_large_interval and test_contains_multiple are based on mathematical facts: if interval length >=2019 or contains a multiple of 2019, answer must be 0. test_small_interval_bruteforce computes the exact answer via brute‑force when feasible (R-L < 2019) and compares. test_consecutive checks the only pair when R==L+1. test_nonzero_no_multiple verifies that a non‑zero answer implies no multiple of 2019 in [L,R]. test_upper_bound_consecutive_small uses a cheap upper bound (min of consecutive products) that is always valid. test_achievable_small verifies that the output appears among all pairs when interval is small enough to enumerate. test_sample matches the given example. Where the plan is vague (e.g., "if the output is not 0, then there cannot be a multiple"), we turn it into a check that uses the input to verify that condition. All tests run in bounded time, and each calls run exactly once.",
