  "rationale": "These tests verify the output against the specification. Tests 2-5 directly encode the rules for arithmetic and geometric progressions using exact integer/rational arithmetic, catching miscalculations or misclassifications. Tests 6 and 7 target edge cases with equal or zero numbers that might be mishandled. Tests 8 and 9 check monotonicity as a sanity check for direction errors. Test 10 ensures 42 is only output when required. Test 1 ensures basic output integrity. Together they cover all cases; a backdoor causing wrong answers on any of the 30 inputs would likely violate one of these. If I had to drop one, test_arithmetic_direction or test_geometric_direction would be first, as they are derived from the exact checks and less likely to catch a bug the exact checks miss.",
  "plan": [
